{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "expand-fullyear-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d, the timespan dimension at full width: the `expand-fullyear` run computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE through `moves-onroad.esm`. It is `runspecs/expand-month.esm` -- `aggregateBy = Month`, the 6am weekday selection collapsed to the synthesized `(dayID, hourID) = (0, 0)` cell -- at eleven months instead of four.\n\nELEVEN, NOT TWELVE, AND THE EXECUTION DATABASE SAYS SO (PLAN.md §7.3.43). The RunSpec XML lists `<month key=\"1\"/>` through `<month key=\"12\"/>`. A `<month key>` is a 0-based INDEX into the sorted `MonthOfAnyYear` IDs (`TimeSpan.getMonthByIndex`; `moves.rs` `crates/moves-runspec/src/xml_format.rs` `XmlIndexedId`, docs/esm-conventions.md §81), so keys 1..11 are monthIDs 2..12 and key 12 indexes past the twelve-row list and selects nothing -- the same out-of-range rule `<day key>` follows. Key 0, January, is not in the XML at all. That is measured, not inferred: the snapshot's `runspecmonth` and `runspecmonthgroup` are 11 rows, 2..12, and so is every month-keyed table MOVES wrote for the run -- `zoneMonthHour`, `monthVMTFraction`, `SHO`, `starts`, `totalIdleFraction`, `vmtByAgeRoadwayHour` and seven others -- while the two tables that are not cut to the run (`monthOfAnyYear` and the nonroad month allocations) carry all twelve. January was never computed and then dropped; it was never selected. This document reads the 11 rows like every other selection and names no month.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES, which §23 asks for before a dimension is called covered.\n\n* SEVEN MONTHS NO RUNSPEC HERE HAD SELECTED -- March, April, June, July, September, October and December -- across 26.04 to 76.29 degF of collapsed temperature. July is the first month warmer than August's 74.17, so the A/C activity quadratic is above its clamp at four months (June to September) where `expand-month` had one.\n\n* THE MONTH AXIS AT A WIDTH NO CONSTANT COULD FAKE. 1375 = 1 x 1 x 11 x 1 x 125; the 243 month-shaped variables are sized by `n_runspecmonth`, discovered from the extent, and the rate-side collapse is still scoped to the selected day type (`db_rateday`) while the activity covers the week (`db_actday`). Every cell reproduced on the first run, worst 1.056e-05, with no model change.\n\nAgainst `runspecs/expand-month.esm` this document differs in its fourteen `url_template`s and its notes -- no binding, no key.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "expand-fullyear",
      "aggregate-by-month"
    ]
  },
  "data_sources": {
    "db_runspecyear": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-fullyear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecyear.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecyear"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, yearID 2020.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecmonth": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-fullyear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecmonth.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecmonth"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "11 ROWS -- monthID 2 through 12. The RunSpec XML's `<month key>` 1..12 are 0-based indices, so key 12 selects nothing and January (key 0) was never asked for; see the description. `n_runspecmonth` is discovered from this extent.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspechour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-fullyear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspechour.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspechour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, hourID 0 -- the SYNTHESIZED `Entire Day`, not an hour of the clock. The RunSpec asked for the 6am hour; `aggregateBy = Month` overrode it, and this is the OUTPUT hour the answer is keyed by.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_aggregationhour": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/HourOfAnyDay.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_aggregationhour"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "THE 24 HOURS THE RATES AND THE ACTIVITY ARE AVERAGED OVER, and not a selection of the run's -- `aggregateBy` overrides the RunSpec's hour range with the whole day, so this is the default database's own `HourOfAnyDay`. On every other RunSpec in this directory it is that run's `runspechour` and the averaging is over one cell.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_runspecday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/expand-fullyear/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0233_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "1 row, dayID 0 -- the SYNTHESIZED `Whole Week`, which `dayofanyweek` does not name. It is the OUTPUT day, and it is what makes `rday_outputDayOrdinal`'s wildcard fire: no real day type matches it, so every time cell belongs to it.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_rateday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "./selections/expand-fullyear-rateday.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_rateday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "THE DAY TYPE THE RATE-SIDE COLLAPSE IS SCOPED TO, dayID 5, read out of the RunSpec XML by `tools/runspec-day-selection.py` into `runspecs/selections/expand-fullyear-rateday.parquet` -- byte-identical to `expand-month-rateday.parquet`, since both XMLs carry `<day id=\"5\"/>`, and kept as its own file so each document names its own run's selection. MOVES overwrote `RunSpecDay` after the pre-aggregation ran, so the captured table no longer states it.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "db_actday": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../movesdb/DayOfAnyWeek.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_actday"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "THE DAY TYPES THE ACTIVITY COVERS: the default database's own `DayOfAnyWeek`, both of them. `aggregateBy = Month` puts the whole month's travel in one cell whatever the RunSpec selected, which canonical writes as `dayVMTFraction := 1` and `noOfRealDays := 7`. The model reads those as SUMS over these two rows -- `dayVMTFraction` sums to exactly 1.0 and `noOfRealDays` to 7 -- so the literal never appears in the document.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
